## Chapter 5: The Assessment Clash
The sudden screech of the emergency sirens shattered the cold morning air at 0500 hours.
Kaelen was out of his bunk before the second blast finished sounding. Around him, his roommates panicked, tumbling out of bed and scrambling for their boots.
Ten minutes later, all eighty freshmen of Anvil Ridge stood lined up on the frost-covered asphalt of the main courtyard. Instructor Horgan stood before them, a thick tablet clutched in his flesh hand while his cybernetic arm clicked as he adjusted his heavy tactical vest.
"Listen up," Horgan barked, his raspy voice cutting through the fog. "The Municipal System Node just flagged a Category-1 breach in Sector 7's abandoned rail yard. A pack of **Iron-Claw Raptors** broke through the containment barrier. The Vanguard already cleared the primary Alpha beast, but the perimeter is littered with secondary stragglers."
A collective murmur of dread ran through the ranks.
"Silence!" Horgan shouted. "City protocol requires all local academies to provide auxiliary containment support. We are being deployed alongside the second-year cadets from **Gideon Prep**."
The mention of Gideon Prep made several students wince. Gideon was a mid-tier private academy located just across the district line—a school full of wealthy Tier-C and Tier-B students who viewed Anvil Ridge as little more than a colony of servants.
"Your task is simple," Horgan continued, glaring at them. "You will set up the perimeter traps, haul the supply crates, and secure the perimeter while Gideon’s combat units flush out the stragglers. You do not engage unless cornered. You do not try to play hero. If you see a monster, you flag it on your radio and fall back."
He tapped his tablet, broadcasting the operation details to their wrist monitors.
"Move out to the transport trucks. And don't embarrass me."
An hour later, Sector 7’s rail yard looked like a warzone. Shattered freight cars lay scattered across overgrown tracks, covered in thick frost and patches of steaming, acidic purple slime.
Kaelen moved quietly along the northern perimeter wall, carrying a heavy box of perimeter motion sensors. Beside him, three Gideon Prep students in pristine, silver-trimmed tactical armor marched with their weapons drawn. Leading them was a tall kid named Vance—a Tier-B *Flame Striker* whose leather coat bore the glowing emblem of a corporate sponsor.
"Hey, Scrapper!" Vance called out without turning around, snapping his fingers lazily. "Set those sensor nodes ten meters apart along the treeline. And make it quick. We’re moving into the inner yard to claim the kill bounties."
"Understood," Kaelen said, keeping his voice meek and slightly breathless as he dragged the crate through the mud.
While the Gideon students moved ahead, talking loudly about their combat stats and showing off their glowing weapon enchantments, Kaelen’s eyes swept the shadowed treeline. His **[Low-Light Spatial Perception]** was active, picking up faint heat traces hidden beneath the dense underbrush.
There weren't just "secondary stragglers" in the treeline. There was a pack. And they were circling behind the Gideon squad's flank.
*Screeech!*
A terrifying, metallic shriek tore through the air as three **Iron-Claw Raptors** leaped from the tree canopy. They were six feet tall, covered in razor-sharp obsidian scales, with long, scythe-like claws made of reinforced bone density.
**[Monster Identification: Iron-Claw Raptor (Tier-D)]**
 * **Attributes:** High Kinetic Speed, Razor-Sharp Physical Density, Pack Coordination.
"Ambush!" one of the Gideon students shrieked, panicking as he fumbled with his shield.
The lead Raptor slammed into him, its heavy claws tearing through his enchanted armor like paper, throwing him hard into a rusted boxcar. The second Raptor lunged straight for Vance, who barely managed to fire a weak blast of flame that only angered the beast further.
The third Raptor—the largest of the pack, its hide glowing with a dark amber hue—snarled, its sickly yellow eyes locking onto Kaelen, who was standing alone by the supply crates.
It saw an easy target. A broke kid in a dirty uniform with no armor and no weapon.
The Raptor lunged, blurring through the air with terrifying speed, its razor claws aimed directly at Kaelen’s throat.
Kaelen didn't scream. He didn't run.
*Finally,* he thought. *A Tier-D.*
The world seemed to slow down as Kaelen’s **[Low-Light Spatial Perception]** tracked the trajectory of the beast's attack. To anyone else, the Raptor was a blur of lethal kinetic force. To Kaelen, with his **21 Agility**, its movement was predictable, heavy, and telegraphed.
At the very last microsecond, as the creature's claws came within inches of his neck, Kaelen shifted his body back just half an inch.
The lethal claws whistled past his chest, cutting only empty air.
Before the Raptor could land, Kaelen dropped his shoulder, dipped beneath its center of gravity, and drove a bare, closed fist straight up into the soft flesh of the beast's exposed underbelly.
He didn't just punch. He channeled every ounce of his **18 Strength** and his **[Dense Fiber Network]** into a single, compact point of impact.
*BOOM!*
A sickening, heavy impact echoed through the rail yard. The Raptor's eyes nearly bulged out of its sockets as the raw, unclassified kinetic force shattered its internal organs and broke its spine in two. The two-hundred-pound monster didn't just stop—it was launched three feet backward into the mud, twitching violently once before going completely still.
**[Target Neutralized: Iron-Claw Raptor (Tier-D)]**
**[Executing Core Skill: Deconstruct...]**
Kaelen didn't hesitate. While Vance and the remaining Gideon student were busy screaming and firing wildly at the other two Raptors ten meters away, Kaelen stepped over the dying creature and pressed his palm flat against its amber hide.
"**[Deconstruct]**," he commanded in his mind.
The dark gray vapor exploded from his skin, devouring the beast's massive carcass in seconds. The flesh, bone, and obsidian scales melted into ash, leaving behind a thick, glowing amber crystal—a pure **Tier-D Attribute Shard**.
**[Unmapped Architectural Parameter Triggered.]**
**[Purification Complete (Efficiency: 100%).]**
**[Absorb Purified Attribute Shard: Iron-Hide Density (Tier-D)?]**
"Absorb," Kaelen growled.
The amber crystal dissolved, shooting straight into his bloodstream like a syringe of molten lead.
*AAARGH!*
The agonizing feedback hit him tenfold compared to the Imp shards. His skin felt like it was being scorched off, his muscle fibers tearing apart and reconstructing into dense, armor-like structures. His ribs cracked and reset, expanding to accommodate his rewired vital organs.
He bit his tongue so hard he tasted copper, forcing his body to stand upright while the brutal transformation raged inside him.
Then, the System interface detonated in his vision with bright, cascading notifications.
**[Structural Assimilation Complete!]**
**[Your baseline attributes have crossed the Critical Threshold!]**
**[LEVEL UP!]**
**[Level 1 ➔ Level 3]**
**[Kaelen Vance]**
 * **Class:** Salvager (Tier-E)
 * **Level:** 3
 * **Strength:** **26 (+8)**
 * **Agility:** **27 (+6)**
 * **Vitality:** **28 (+9)**
 * **Aetheric Resonance:** **8 (+4)**
**[Skill Evolution Triggered!]**
 * **[Deconstruct (Lv.2)]** ➔ **[Dissect & Assimilate (Lv.1)]**
   * *Effect: Efficiency increased to 75%. Allows the user to forcibly extract and permanently store ONE active combat skill from a defeated Tier-D or higher target.*
**[New Active Skill Acquired!]**
 * **[Iron-Claw Burst (Tier-D)]** - *Instantly hardens the user's upper limbs with kinetic density, delivering a devastating blunt strike that ignores 30% of the target's physical armor. (Cooldown: 15s).*
**[New Passive Trait Acquired!]**
 * **[Obsidian Carapace (Tier-D)]** - *Sub-dermal tissue hardens upon impact, reducing incoming physical cutting and piercing damage by 35%.*
The rush of raw, unadulterated power flooded every nerve ending in Kaelen’s body. The lingering fatigue of the past three weeks vanished instantly, replaced by a violent, exhilarating surge of energy. He could feel his heart beating with the heavy, steady thud of an iron engine.
He looked down at his right hand. A faint, metallic sheen flickered beneath his skin before vanishing into his flesh.
"Vance! Help!" the Gideon student screamed nearby, his shield breaking under the assault of the second Raptor.
Kaelen let out a slow, controlled breath, instantly suppressing the glowing aura surrounding his body. He slumped his shoulders, took a step back into the shadows of the boxcar, and let his face twist into a look of absolute, terrified panic.
"I-I'm going for help!" Kaelen yelled, his voice cracking with deliberate weakness as he sprinted away into the fog, moving at a fraction of his true speed.
Behind him, Vance yelled an insult, completely unaware that the Tier-E "garbage man" had just killed a Tier-D beast with his bare hands, stolen its power, and evolved into something that could crush his skull like an eggshell.
